31,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n DC generator schematic is shown in figure</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/909e99b454b1c78597a528b345993495ab59b801.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/c0248fa9333a49d07a2f8e5e137b927de7f00eeb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n If time constant of the system is to be made 20 msec, then feedback factor required will be ________</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.04","high":"0.06"},"solution":"<p>\n 0.05 (0.04 - 0.06)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/af808024c386f6a4ab9fffcc6defa89f8dc6cd6d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":32,"type":"MSQ","correct":"B,D","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the system shown in figure, with <em>K</em> > 1</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/c88411dd42b52c938d3bf544a806cb694f8c0d28.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n Which of the following statements is/are correct for the system?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> The type of the system is 2.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> The velocity error constant is zero.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> The acceleration error constant is infinite.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n The value of <em>K</em> to yield 0.1% error in the steady state is 1.001.</p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b, d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/081abc47c6ff4dcc30ee702a4ccdad268c64e61a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":33,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n The open loop transfer function of a control system is given by,</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/50db135f1a1df8d2468590d28e495f912c55d84c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n If GM = 6 dB, then <em>K</em> is __________ .</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"119","high":"121"},"solution":"<p>\n 120 (119 - 121)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/8c3c25